---
import BaseLayout from "../../site/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import "../../site/styles/disclosure-study.css";
---

<BaseLayout title="Disclosure study — Mourne Made" description="A visual study of the concept disclosure for Mourne Made." hideFooter>
  <main class="disclosure-study">
    <div class="shell disclosure-study-intro">
      <a class="disclosure-study-back" href="/prototypes/comparison-caption-study/">← Comparison caption study</a>
      <p class="home-kicker">Mourne Made · component study</p>
      <h1>How should the work stay honest?</h1>
      <p class="disclosure-study-lede">Three disclosure treatments for the independent-concept message that appears beside the work.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="shell disclosure-study-grid">
      <article class="disclosure-option"><p class="disclosure-option-name"><span>A</span> Quiet note</p><p class="disclosure-demo disclosure-demo--quiet"><strong>Independent concept.</strong> Created from public information to demonstrate an idea.</p><p>Clear, compact, and easy to read without pulling focus.</p></article>
      <article class="disclosure-option"><p class="disclosure-option-name"><span>B</span> Ruled note</p><p class="disclosure-demo disclosure-demo--rule"><strong>Independent concept.</strong> Created from public information to demonstrate an idea.</p><p>A small yellow rule makes the trust message easier to spot.</p></article>
      <article class="disclosure-option"><p class="disclosure-option-name"><span>C</span> Marked note</p><p class="disclosure-demo disclosure-demo--marked"><b aria-hidden="true">C</b><span><strong>Independent concept.</strong> Created from public information to demonstrate an idea.</span></p><p>A compact mark gives the disclosure a repeatable visual identity.</p></article>
    </div>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
